pel music with the Queen of Gospel, Albertina Walker and the Caravans. \r\nIn 1976 she began singing on Disco productions (mainly on Salsoul Records) and was responsible for some classics like \"Love Sensation\" and \"Relight My Fire\" by [a=Dan Hartman].\r\nIn 1984, Holloway left Salsoul Records and began to work on an album, \"Crash Goes Love\". Unfortunately it was never completed and only two singles were released for Streetwise, the title track and \"Sweet Thing\", a song co-written by Chaka Khan & Tony Maiden of \"Rufus\"... She recorded \"Heartstealer\" whilst in London for Ian Levine (the day after she played \"Heaven\" night club 10th anniversary)!\r\nDuring the following years, many of her old hits were adapted by House producers like [a=Black Box] who sampled her vocals from 1980 disco hit \"Love Sensation\" to their track \"Ride On Time\". Her vocals were originally used without credit, but she successfully sued the band and received an undisclosed share of the royalties. The only time she was properly paid and credited was on the [a=Marky Mark & The Funky Bunch] song \"Good Vibrations\" (1991), which also sampled some of her vocals from \"Love Sensation\".","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:17413","relations":{"aliases":null,"groups":[{"active":true,"id":195204,"name":"Togetherness"}],"members":null,"namevariations":["Featuring","Holloway","L Holloway","L. Holloway","LH","Loietta Holloway","Loleata Holloway","Loleatta","Loleatta Halloway","Loleatta Hathaway","Loleatta Hollaway","Loleatta Hollo Way","Loleatta Hollyoway","Loleatta Holoway","Loleatta Hooloway","Lolehatta Holloway","Loletta","Loletta Halloway","Loletta Holloway","Lolleatha Holloway","Lolleatta Halloway","Lolleatta Holloway","Lolleta Holloway","Lolletta Holloway","Loretta Holloway","Лолетта Холлоуэй","ロリータ・ハラウェイ","ロリータ・ハロウェイ"]},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/17413-Loleatta-Holloway","type":"artist","urls":["http://www.allmusic.com/artist/loleatta-holloway-mn0000829125","http://www.disco-disco.com/artists/loleatta.shtml","http://www.jahsonic.com/LoleattaHolloway.html","http://www.myspace.com/httpwwwloleattaholloway","http://www.soulwalking.co.uk/Loleatta%20Holloway.html","http://www.soundcloud.com/loleatta-holloway","http://www.whosampled.com/Loleatta-Holloway","http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Loleatta_Holloway"]}},"/api/discogs/artist/238372/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"238372","image":"https://i.discogs.com/xbgaXGDIcaeUWGrZL8AwhONP-Yb7Mch358pSdUVQcyo/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:433/w:413/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTIzODM3/Mi0xNzM3MjE3MTM0/LTMxOTIuanBlZw.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/LIxJ473meNfGZ-MNKgJR9hEZktYtsp6ErI9v06F0u58/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTIzODM3/Mi0xNzM3MjE3MTM0/LTMxOTIuanBlZw.jpeg","profile":"American experimental rock group, founded in 2002 in New York City.","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:238372","relations":{"aliases":null,"groups":null,"members":[{"active":true,"id":187429,"name":"Ian Williams"},{"active":true,"id":251525,"name":"John Stanier"},{"active":false,"id":285566,"name":"Tyondai Braxton"},{"active":false,"id":696625,"name":"Dave Konopka"}],"namevariations":["The Battles","バトルス"]},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/238372-Battles","type":"artist","urls":["http://www.bttls.com","https://www.facebook.com/miceparade/","http://www.myspace.com/battlestheband","http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battles_(band)","https://twitter.com/BATTLES","https://www.instagram.com/battlestheband?igsh=MWd3Mm9wODdhejJhYg==","https://battles.bandcamp.com"]}},"/api/discogs/artist/308828/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"308828","image":"","imageThumb":"","profile":"Chicago dance music producer.","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:308828","relations":{"aliases":[{"id":58866,"name":"Chrissy"},{"id":3581265,"name":"Chris E Pants"}],"groups":null,"members":null,"namevariations":["Chrissy","Murderbot"]},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/308828-Chrissy-Murderbot","type":"artist","urls":[]}},"/api/discogs/artist/3183708/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"3183708","image":"https://i.discogs.com/HfEaym9ezW-rX9Pf1ibBwrNe8zbxWVO87jd18_Kb8QY/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:435/w:350/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTMxODM3/MDgtMTM4NzM0MjEz/OS0xNDcyLmpwZWc.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/HaJjtKcgvEBSjMKqbeMkNPZYfXcmxeWkBGev01rmX-c/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTMxODM3/MDgtMTM4NzM0MjEz/OS0xNDcyLmpwZWc.jpeg","profile":"Rapper & vocalist from New York, USA.","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:3183708","relations":{"aliases":[{"id":16913125,"name":"Rashard Caliel Bradshaw"}],"groups":null,"members":null,"namevariations":["Cakes Da Killer"]},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/3183708-Cakes-Da-Killa","type":"artist","urls":["http://cakesdakilla.com/","https://www.facebook.com/Cakes-Da-Killa-149034035175294/","https://www.instagram.com/cakesdakilla/","https://cakesdakilla.bandcamp.com/music"]}},"/api/discogs/artist/3339341/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"3339341","image":"https://i.discogs.com/yLIMKMyFXEFHym6_NpfNcuPcOYtWZaNS7Rbla0FklQs/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:450/w:600/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTMzMzkz/NDEtMTU4NDE2MDYx/NC03Mjc1LmpwZWc.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/qTe4LDfkzRpFFFXJVwdKOIJIM2SnFVEQtAWCvedH3oQ/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTMzMzkz/NDEtMTU4NDE2MDYx/NC03Mjc1LmpwZWc.jpeg","profile":"For the past few years, Ashley Thomas has steadily been building up his artillery of forward thinking, and hard hitting club music under his moniker, Otik.\r\n\r\nAfter releasing on the likes of Polydor, Dusky’s 17 Steps, Infinite Machine, and DEXT Recordings, he debuted a 4-track effort, ‘Top Ten’ EP on Keysound Recordings in late 2018.\r\n\r\nIn 2019 Otik kicked off the year with the compilation track ‘Memoria’ and the ‘Stoned Ghost’ EP on Berlin’s Nous imprint, continuing to explore the emotive and dreamy side of UK Techno. This was soon followed by the vocal club track ‘Actress’ on Midland’s Intergraded, and later the experimental ‘Dioxide’ EP via his staple label DEXT Recordings, including a remix from Hessle Audio’s Bruce. October of 2019 brought the EP ‘Blasphemy’ released by Boogie Box Records, accompanied by a killer remix from Timedance’s Metrist. \r\n\r\n2020 has been a fast paced year for Otik so far and has seen him return to Intergraded for a 4 track solo EP 'Wetlands', which was met with wide critical acclaim and support from across the board. In March he released the single 'NDE' on Hodge & Franklin De Costa's 'Mother's Finest' imprint which was then followed by another 4 track effort for Mr. Mitch's Gobstopper Records in April. With a bunch of releases still to come this year, he doesn't seem to be slowing down just yet.\r\n\r\nOtik’s Techno, Worldly, and Breaks influenced DJ mixes are a guaranteed dance floor filler every time, and he has been praised by the likes of Earmilk & DJ Mag for his “inventive and infectious club sets and radio shows.” With previous mixes on NTS, Rinse FM, Worldwide FM and BBC Radio 1 & 1xtra, he currently delivers a quarterly radio show on Rinse France (with past guests including Cosmin TRG, Andrea, Throwing Snow), attempting to blend the sounds of UK Techno, Weightless, and other experimental & underground music from across the globe.","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:3339341","relations":{"aliases":null,"groups":null,"members":null,"namevariations":null},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/3339341-Otik","type":"artist","urls":["https://otik.bandcamp.com/music","https://soundcloud.com/otikmusic","https://www.instagram.com/ot1k","https://twitter.com/otikulate","https://www.facebook.com/ot1kulate"]}},"/api/discogs/artist/441448/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"4414